LB Closeout #853 — agent_tasks lockdown, ai_interactions linkage proof, kill silent catches

Three independent hardening axes for Level B closeout:

AXE 1 — public.agent_tasks RLS lockdown
- New migration 20260429000000_agent_tasks_lockdown.sql drops the legacy
  agent_tasks_owner_insert and agent_tasks_owner_update policies, REVOKEs
  INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE from authenticated + anon, and stamps a TABLE
  COMMENT making the read-only-projection contract explicit. Idempotent
  via DO/IF EXISTS blocks. SELECT policy + trigger preserved so the UI
  keeps working unchanged. service_role unaffected (RLS bypass).
- New supabase/tests/agent_tasks_lockdown.test.sql proves SELECT still
  works for the owner and INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE are denied.

AXE 2 — ai_interactions linkage proof
- Confirmed via repo-wide grep that the SOLE writer of ai_interactions
  from inside a dispatched run is createSupabaseInteractionSink in
  ai-adapter.ts, which already sets execution_task_id: task.id (no code
  change needed).
- Added a clarifying banner to _shared/ai-cost-tracker.ts warning that
  logAiInteraction is for non-dispatched callsites only.
- New regression test (lb-closeout-853-hardening.test.ts) covers the
  linkage with three cases: standard run, system-initiated run with
  null requested_by, and the failure path that throws InteractionSinkError.

AXE 3 — kill silent catches
- New _shared/structured-error.ts helper exposes emitStructuredError +
  runOrLog with a stable `{level, event, message, stack, ...}` envelope.
- Replaced 4 bare `catch (_) {}` swallows with structured console.error
  emissions:
    * engine-cron-server.ts heartbeat → engine_cron.supervisor_upsert_failed
    * engine-cron-server.ts fx-refresh → engine_cron.fx_refresh_failed
    * pipeline-worker.ts validate stage → pipeline_worker.validate_firewall_log_failed
    * pipeline-worker.ts publish stage  → pipeline_worker.publish_firewall_log_failed
- Test suite asserts no remaining `catch (_) {}` in those two files and
  validates structured envelope shape.

